{{Quote|And you must take a day trip to the to the Holographic Museum of Extinct Animals. There are some truly fascinating creatures on display. I found the mantabog of Malastare to be utterly&hellip; Ah. Look at that, here we are. Amnesty Housing.|A taxi droid|audio=CabbieDroid-Mantabog-M19.flac|<ref name="Convert" />}}
The '''Holographic Museum of Extinct Animals''' was a [[museum]] in [[Imperial City|Galactic City]], the [[ecumenopolis]] that covered<ref name="Convert" /> the [[Core Worlds]]<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. It displayed several extinct creatures, including the [[mantabog]] of<ref name="Convert" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> [[Malastare]].<ref name="Convert" /> Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|19}}</ref> a [[Unidentified taxi droid|taxi droid]] recommended a [[Standard day|day]] trip to the museum to [[Doctor]] [[Penn Pershing]], a new arrival to Corsucant that the [[Taxi droid|droid]] was driving from the [[Galaxies Opera House]] to [[Amnesty Housing]]. The [[droid]] claimed to have found several of the creatures on display at the museum fascinating and began to speak about the mantabog before the conversation was interrupted by their arrival at the housing's landing bay.<ref name="Convert" />

==Behind the scenes==
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the Holographic Museum of Extinct Animals was mentioned in "[[Chapter 19: The Convert]]," the third episode of the [[Disney+]] show [[Star Wars: The Mandalorian|''The Mandalorian's'']] [[The Mandalorian Season Three|third season]],<ref name="Convert" /> which aired on [[March 15]], [[2023]].<ref name="D23 March">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-march-2023|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in March 2023}}</ref> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, it was named the [[Holographic Zoo of Extinct Animals]], and first appeared in the [[1994]] novel ''[[Dark Apprentice (novel)|Dark Apprentice]]'' by [[Kevin J. Anderson]].<ref name="DarkApprentice">[[Dark Apprentice (novel)|''Dark Apprentice'']]</ref> It was then depicted in the [[Qui-Gon and Obi-Wan: Last Stand on Ord Mantell 1|first issue]] of the [[Star Wars: Qui-Gon and Obi-Wan: Last Stand on Ord Mantell|''Qui-Gon and Obi-Wan: Last Stand on Ord Mantell'']] [[Star Wars comic books|comic-book]] series, which was written by [[Ryder Windham]], illustrated by [[Ramón F. Bachs]],<ref name="OrdMantell">[[Qui-Gon and Obi-Wan: Last Stand on Ord Mantell 1|''Qui-Gon and Obi-Wan: Last Stand on Ord Mantell'' 1]]</ref> and published on [[December 20]], [[2000]].<ref name="Marvel">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/54469/star_wars_qui-gon_obi-wan_-_last_stand_on_ord_mantell_2000_1|text=Star Wars: Qui-Gon & Obi-Wan - Last Stand on Ord Mantell (2000) #1}}</ref>

